-- title:
--   Complete DVR with uniformiser and residues from A is widehatA
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring (a commutative ring which is a domain and a discrete valuation ring in the Mathlib sense), and let $\varpi \in A$ be an element with $\mathfrak{m}_A = (\varpi)$, i.e. the maximal ideal of the local ring $A$ is the ideal generated by $\varpi$. Let $W$ be a further commutative ring which is a domain and a discrete valuation ring, and assume $W$ is complete (and separated) for the $\mathfrak{m}_W$-adic topology, where $\mathfrak{m}_W$ is the maximal ideal of $W$. Let $\sigma \colon A \to W$ be a ring homomorphism such that $\mathfrak{m}_W = (\sigma\varpi)$, the ideal of $W$ generated by the image of $\varpi$, and such that every $w \in W$ is congruent modulo $\mathfrak{m}_W$ to some element of the image of $\sigma$, i.e. for each $w$ there is $a \in A$ with $w - \sigma a \in \mathfrak{m}_W$. The conclusion is that there exists a ring isomorphism $\rho \colon W \xrightarrow{\sim} \widehat{A}$ onto the $\mathfrak{m}_A$-adic completion of $A$ such that $\rho(\sigma a)$ equals the canonical image of $a$ in $\widehat{A}$ under the structure map $A \to \widehat{A}$, for every $a \in A$.
--
--   This is the standard recognition criterion for the completion of a discrete valuation ring: a complete discrete valuation ring receiving $A$ so that a uniformiser goes to a uniformiser and the residue map is surjective is canonically identified with $\widehat{A}$ over $A$. It is used in the work on models of modular curves to replace the coefficient ring of a local chart witness by $\widehat{A}$ itself, so that node-ring presentations of the ends can be written over the completion.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsDiscreteValuationRing_exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_apply_eq_algebraMap_of_maximalIdeal_eq_span_map_of_forall_exists_sub_mem.lean

